From 5aee1e9f2433204e4acb6ecf30300124d5629365 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:59:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] panvk/csf: count, prefix sum and draw a tess chunk in one
 workgroup

Each tessellation chunk ran three dependent dispatches after the TCS,
each followed by a full compute drain: panlib_tessellate(COUNT),
panlib_tess_draw() (a serial prefix sum on a single invocation, one
dependent load/store per patch, up to ~507 patches a chunk) and
panlib_tessellate(WITH_COUNTS) (tess perf review #2, #3).

panlib_tess_count_draw() does COUNT, a 64-wide workgroup scan of the
per-patch index counts and the draw/range bookkeeping of
panlib_tess_draw() in one workgroup. For a direct draw with at most
PANVK_TESS_FUSE_GEN_MAX patches (default 64), the same workgroup also
runs the WITH_COUNTS pass after a global barrier: the separate pass
would have been a single 64-wide workgroup too, so nothing is lost,
and the chunk takes one dispatch instead of three. Larger and
indirect draws keep the many-workgroup WITH_COUNTS pass.

Statistics, prims-generated, range and "more" are written exactly as
panlib_tess_draw() writes them. The kernels live in a new
libpan/tess_fast.cl (with panlib_tess_gen(), the WITH_COUNTS pass), so
draw_helper.cl and the v9 JM tess path that later series patch stay as
they are.

PANVK_TESS_FUSE=0 restores the three passes. Both knobs are read at
VkDevice creation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
